"P2684535331" "The soul of Red Widow"
// DetailString :
"P4287243842" "This clear crystal is lit by a reddish light, and contains the captured soul of the Red Widow. You have to wonder whether holding this thing is entirely safe."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - FakeCrystal 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P3595588952" "A false soul"
// DetailString :
"P1515437798" "This Circle of Thorns soul crystal contains one soul. You hear the anguished cry of an innocent woman when you touch it, but it is not the Red Widow. Rather, it's some poor victim of Arachnos used to make this false crystal."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - GhostWidowPossession 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2025828372" "Ghost Widow's possessions"
// DetailString :
"P1742402346" "A few hair ribbons, a black cloak, and some gushing letters written to Lord Recluse are all the possessions Ghost Widow has left of her mortal life. You have to wonder why she saved them."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - EpisodeOneClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P360694964" "Life and Death"
// DetailString :
"P2619951018" "It began when Ghost Widow told you she had grown tired of her spectral life. She wanted to become human again, and she suspected the Circle of Thorns would know a way to do it. You scoured the streets for the mages, and eventually learned that the secrets might lie in the Tome of Tormvodel. "

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - EpisodeTwoClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P1421190728" "It began when Ghost Widow told you she had grown tired of her spectral life. She wanted to become human again, and she suspected the Circle of Thorns would know a way to do it. You scoured the streets for the mages, and eventually learned that the secrets might lie in the Tome of Tormvodel. <br><br>You stole the tome from a Circle base, and Ghost Widow prepared to work her magic. "

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - EpisodeThreeClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P1975522950" "It began when Ghost Widow told you she had grown tired of her spectral life. She wanted to become human again, and she suspected the Circle of Thorns would know a way to do it. You scoured the streets for the mages, and eventually learned that the secrets might lie in the Tome of Tormvodel. <br><br>You stole the tome from a Circle base, and Ghost Widow prepared to work her magic. <br><br>But she wanted to test the ritual first. She sent you to gather some artifacts of another spirit's life. "

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - EpisodeFourClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P3616181262" "It began when Ghost Widow told you she had grown tired of her spectral life. She wanted to become human again, and she suspected the Circle of Thorns would know a way to do it. You scoured the streets for the mages, and eventually learned that the secrets might lie in the Tome of Tormvodel. <br><br>You stole the tome from a Circle base, and Ghost Widow prepared to work her magic. <br><br>But she wanted to test the ritual first. She sent you to gather some artifacts of another spirit's life. <br><br>You gathered the items, and learned that Ghost Widow's target was none other than Red Widow, one of Lord Recluse's most trusted assassins. You performed the ceremony, but instead of restoring Red Widow to life, you used a soul crystal to trap her. "

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - EpisodeFiveClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P3248892758" "It began when Ghost Widow told you she had grown tired of her spectral life. She wanted to become human again, and she suspected the Circle of Thorns would know a way to do it. You scoured the streets for the mages, and eventually learned that the secrets might lie in the Tome of Tormvodel. <br><br>You stole the tome from a Circle base, and Ghost Widow prepared to work her magic. <br><br>But she wanted to test the ritual first. She sent you to gather some artifacts of another spirit's life. <br><br>You gathered the items, and learned that Ghost Widow's target was none other than Red Widow, one of Lord Recluse's most trusted assassins. You performed the ceremony, but instead of restoring Red Widow to life, you used a soul crystal to trap her. <br><br>Ghost Widow was ready to work the spell on herself, but first you were summoned before Arbiter Daos. He informed you that Ghost Widow's actions had incurred the ire of Lord Recluse. If you wished to drag yourself out of the hole she had dug, you would not help Ghost Widow; instead, you would punish her. Daos first had you recover the Red Widow's soul from one of Ghost Widow's bases. Once this was done, he had a final task for you: He wants you to defeat Ghost Widow when she tries to re-form herself, destroying her new body and returning her to her spectral form."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef - SL8_GhostWidow_Storyarc3 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef Name :
"P2624521599" "Daos' seal"
// tDetailString :
"P515357387" "After you obeyed his command to punish Ghost Widow for her actions against Red Widow, Arbiter Daos gave you this seal. It's a mark of distinction within Arachnos, as well as a reminder of the adventure you like to call: <br><br>Life and Death <br><br>It began when Ghost Widow told you she had grown tired of her spectral life. She wanted to become human again, and she suspected the Circle of Thorns would know a way to do it. You scoured the streets for the mages, and eventually learned that the secrets might lie in the Tome of Tormvodel. <br><br>You stole the tome from a Circle base, and Ghost Widow prepared to work her magic. <br><br>But she wanted to test the ritual first. She sent you to gather some artifacts of another spirit's life. <br><br>You gathered the items, and learned that Ghost Widow's target was none other than Red Widow, one of Lord Recluse's most trusted assassins. You performed the ceremony, but instead of restoring Red Widow to life, you used a soul crystal to trap her. <br><br>Ghost Widow was ready to work the spell on herself, but first you were summoned before Arbiter Daos. He informed you that Ghost Widow's actions had incurred the ire of Lord Recluse. If you wished to drag yourself out of the hole she had dug, you would not help Ghost Widow; instead, you would punish her. Daos first had you recover the Red Widow's soul from one of Ghost Widow's bases. Once this was done, he had a final task for you: He wants you to defeat Ghost Widow when she tries to re-form herself, destroying her new body and returning her to her spectral form. <br><br>Your relationship with Ghost Widow has taken a serious hit, but you're not too concerned about it. After all, you are a villain who has bested Ghost Widow. Surely her wrath means little to you now."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Errand1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P3247661887" "We've worked together for a while, you and I, and I think you have proven that I can trust you to help me, in even the most delicate of matters. Tell me, {VillainName}, have you ever wondered what it would be like to be a ghost? Immortal, untouchable, unchanging. By some standards, a perfect being. I won't deny that my existence has its benefits, but still I long to be human again. I can't help it. The dead cannot change, and when you are dying you want nothing more than life. And now I may have found a way to return from this state and live once again. This is what I have been working towards. <A HREF={ACCEPT}>{VillainName}, I want your help to bring me back to life.</A>"
// AcceptString :
"P3445527062" "Help Ghost Widow get her body back"
// SendOffString :
"P3891283147" "I am close to developing a ritual that will help me reclaim my body, but I need some more information from the Circle of Thorns. Seek them out, and force them to tell you about a book called the Tome of Tormvodel."
// ActiveTaskString :
"P2077206263" "Question Circle mages"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P3333011162" "If the Circle has the tome, then I will be on the verge of a new life."
// Script Variable LOITER_ATTACK_TEXT :
"P856364347" ""

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P1004145216" "One of the mystics you defeated told you what you wanted to know."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
